        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "PWM mode: each servo header's signal pin gets its own independent 1 kΩ-buffered GPIO line ... leave R13/R14 open; Serial mode: populate R13/R14 (page 1/1, sheet /)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "As drawn, the servo signal paths are connected to the shared serial bus through the zero-ohm links rather than being independently selectable as specified. This can prevent independent PWM control and cause interference or contention between the PWM GPIOs and the serial interface.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The servo-mode jumper implementation contradicts the specified routing: R1/R4 are shown as 0 Ω links into the shared serial bus, while the annotated R13/R14 positions are occupied by nonzero resistors elsewhere in the circuit. This joins the signal paths instead of providing the specified selectable PWM-versus-serial configuration."
}

